1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:03,337
Before you code an interview or quote a participant, you need to

2
00:00:03,337 --> 00:00:04,753
check what was actually said.

3
00:00:05,137 --> 00:00:09,119
Transcript Review Studio helps you do that on your own computer.

4
00:00:09,667 --> 00:00:14,159
It uses local speech-to-text to generate multiple candidate transcripts.

5
00:00:14,450 --> 00:00:18,932
It compares their wording and uses model confidence scores to highlight

6
00:00:18,932 --> 00:00:22,659
passages that may need a closer listen, helping you focus your

7
00:00:22,659 --> 00:00:23,633
review.

8
00:00:24,167 --> 00:00:26,802
But you can review any part of the recording, including moments

9
00:00:26,802 --> 00:00:28,381
the AI hasn't flagged.

10
00:00:28,933 --> 00:00:32,776
Watch the video, replay a sentence, compare the versions, and edit

11
00:00:32,776 --> 00:00:33,623
as you listen.

12
00:00:34,007 --> 00:00:38,105
Correct the words, label the speaker, or leave an uncertain passage

13
00:00:38,105 --> 00:00:39,091
for later.

14
00:00:39,633 --> 00:00:43,662
When you're ready for qualitative analysis, export a Word transcript,

15
00:00:43,662 --> 00:00:46,587
an NVivo-style table, or a spreadsheet.

16
00:00:47,133 --> 00:00:50,035
Keep a before-and-after record of your corrections, so colleagues

17
00:00:50,035 --> 00:00:51,440
can see what changed.

18
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:53,950
Speech recognition runs locally.

19
00:00:54,171 --> 00:00:56,911
The app does not upload your recordings or transcripts to cloud

20
00:00:56,911 --> 00:00:57,979
services.

21
00:00:58,533 --> 00:01:01,552
Try the included sample, follow the walkthrough, and bring in your

22
00:01:01,552 --> 00:01:02,700
next interview.
